1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,720
You will hear a woman phoning a
car share club to become a member.

2
00:00:04,619 --> 00:00:08,140
First, you have some time
to look at questions 1 to 7.

3
00:00:38,629 --> 00:00:42,880
How can I help?

4
00:00:42,881 --> 00:00:46,000
Oh, hi Craig.
I'd like to join the club please.

5
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:50,100
The online form kept freezing
on me, so I thought I'd just ring.

6
00:00:50,295 --> 00:00:54,080
Yeah, sorry about that.
No worries, I can do it over the phone.

7
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,520
Can I start with your name?

8
00:00:55,809 --> 00:00:57,640
Sure, it's Joanna Pello.

9
00:00:58,110 --> 00:00:59,960
And how do you spell the surname?

10
00:01:00,599 --> 00:01:05,760
P-E-L-L-O-W-E

11
00:01:06,159 --> 00:01:10,420
P-E-L-L-O-W

12
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:14,720
Sorry, there's an E on the end as well.
People always leave it off.

13
00:01:14,970 --> 00:01:18,020
Got it, with the E. And your home address?

14
00:01:18,364 --> 00:01:21,840
It's Flat 6, 42 Lenox Street in Roselle.

15
00:01:22,339 --> 00:01:24,860
Lenox Street. And the postcode?

16
00:01:26,319 --> 00:01:31,900
2039. No, hang on.
That's the office. Home is 2037.

17
00:01:33,820 --> 00:01:37,716
2037. Lovely. Now, we ask
everyone what they'll mainly

18
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:41,432
be using the cars for. Is
it mostly for work or...?

19
00:01:50,859 --> 00:01:54,674
Not for work, no. I cycle to the office. I used to borrow a friend's car
to take my sister to the airport, but she's moved to Perth now. So, these

20
00:01:54,698 --> 00:01:58,725
days, it'd mostly be to drive up and see my grandmother. She lives in a
little town in the Blue Mountains, and the train doesn't go all the way.

21
00:01:58,749 --> 00:02:01,737
Yeah, the trains up there
aren't great at weekends.

22
00:02:01,761 --> 00:02:06,492
And which of our car bays would be handiest
for you? In Roselle, we've got three.

23
00:02:06,529 --> 00:02:09,420
Well, the one at the light
rail stop would be ideal.

24
00:02:09,444 --> 00:02:13,267
But every time I've looked on the
map, the cars there are booked out.

25
00:02:13,268 --> 00:02:15,260
That one's very popular, I'm afraid.

26
00:02:15,261 --> 00:02:20,540
And the bay outside the library.
I thought that'd be the closest, but...

27
00:02:20,690 --> 00:02:23,205
Ah, that one's actually
closed till the end of the year.

28
00:02:23,229 --> 00:02:25,047
The council's digging
up the road there.

29
00:02:25,048 --> 00:02:28,646
Right. Then put me down for
the one behind the swimming pool.

30
00:02:28,670 --> 00:02:31,352
It's only a five-minute
walk, so that's fine.

31
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:36,160
Behind the pool, no problem. You can
change that any time in the app anyway.

32
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:39,561
Now, we've got three
plans. There's Casual, which

33
00:02:39,585 --> 00:02:42,472
has no monthly fee,
but higher hourly rates.

34
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:46,402
There's Plus, which has a small
monthly fee and cheaper hours.

35
00:02:46,426 --> 00:02:50,012
And Premium, which is really
for people who drive most days.

36
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:56,000
I was thinking Casual, because I honestly
won't drive that much. Maybe twice a month?

37
00:02:56,350 --> 00:02:59,920
You could, but two return
trips to the mountains a month?

38
00:02:59,944 --> 00:03:03,212
They're long bookings.
Say, six or seven hours each.

39
00:03:03,910 --> 00:03:06,818
On Casual, you'd be paying
the higher rate the whole time.

40
00:03:06,842 --> 00:03:09,612
I reckon the middle one
would work out cheaper for you.

41
00:03:10,050 --> 00:03:14,000
Hmm. Yeah, if they're full day trips...

42
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:18,960
Okay, you've talked me into it.
I'll go for Plus. Not Premium, though.

43
00:03:18,961 --> 00:03:20,960
That's way more than I need.

44
00:03:20,961 --> 00:03:22,960
Fair enough. Plus it is.

45
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:26,960
And what's the monthly fee on that?
The website said $12.50.

46
00:03:27,410 --> 00:03:31,740
Ah, that's last year's figure.
The page hasn't been updated.

47
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:34,972
It went up in July. It's
$14.95 a month now.

48
00:03:35,260 --> 00:03:39,960
$14.95. Okay. Still a lot cheaper
than running my own car.

49
00:03:40,110 --> 00:03:43,907
Definitely. Now, we'll need a
scan of your driver's license, front

50
00:03:43,931 --> 00:03:47,972
and back, and something showing
your address. A bank statement's fine.

51
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:51,106
I don't get paper statements
anymore. It's all online.

52
00:03:51,130 --> 00:03:53,972
And the screenshots don't
actually show my address.

53
00:03:54,310 --> 00:03:57,716
Right. We used to take
mobile phone bills, but we can't

54
00:03:57,740 --> 00:04:00,972
accept those anymore.
Head office changed the rules.

55
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,960
Have you got a gas or an electricity bill?

56
00:04:02,961 --> 00:04:05,948
The gas is in my flatmate's
name, but I can send you my

57
00:04:05,972 --> 00:04:08,967
electricity bill. That's got
my name and address on it.

58
00:04:08,968 --> 00:04:11,960
Perfect.
Just email it to us with the license scan.

59
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:15,748
Before you hear the
rest of the conversation,

60
00:04:15,772 --> 00:04:18,971
you have some time to
look at questions 8 to 10.

61
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:52,960
Can I ask about the rules? What
happens if I'm late bringing a car back?

62
00:04:54,310 --> 00:04:57,960
The traffic coming down from the
mountains can be awful on a Sunday night.

63
00:04:58,310 --> 00:05:01,654
It happens. If you can,
extend the booking in the app

64
00:05:01,678 --> 00:05:04,972
before it runs out. If you
don't, there is a charge.

65
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:08,123
It used to be a flat $25.
Whatever happened?

66
00:05:08,147 --> 00:05:11,972
Which people thought was a bit
harsh if they were only 5 minutes over.

67
00:05:11,973 --> 00:05:13,960
I can imagine.

68
00:05:15,960 --> 00:05:19,903
So now it's worked out in blocks of 15 minutes.
You pay a small fee for each block you're

69
00:05:19,927 --> 00:05:23,972
over. We don't charge you for a whole extra
hour, which is what some of the other clubs do.

70
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:27,023
That sounds fairer. And
is there anything I have

71
00:05:27,047 --> 00:05:29,972
to do before I drive off?
Do I need to ring you?

72
00:05:35,960 --> 00:05:39,962
You don't need to call us. That's what we used to ask, but the app
does all that now. Some members check the petrol gauge, but honestly,

73
00:05:39,986 --> 00:05:43,972
our staff refuel the cars, and there's a fuel card in the glove box
if you do run low. So that's not something you need to worry about.

74
00:05:43,961 --> 00:05:44,961
Oh, right.

75
00:05:46,060 --> 00:05:50,068
The one thing we do insist on is that you
walk around the car and take pictures of any

76
00:05:50,092 --> 00:05:53,972
scratches or dents in the app. Otherwise,
you could end up getting blamed for them.

77
00:05:54,110 --> 00:05:55,960
Good to know. I'll make sure I do that.

78
00:05:55,985 --> 00:05:58,178
So, would you like to make
your first booking now?

79
00:05:58,202 --> 00:06:00,972
Your membership card takes
about five days to come in the post.

80
00:06:00,973 --> 00:06:03,960
Oh, so I'd have to wait for that anyway?

81
00:06:03,961 --> 00:06:07,345
No, no. You don't need the card.
Once your documents are approved,

82
00:06:07,369 --> 00:06:10,972
you can unlock the cards with your
phone. That's usually the same day.

83
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:13,960
Oh, good.
I was hoping to go up this Saturday.

84
00:06:14,410 --> 00:06:18,960
Let me see. Yep. The hatchback
behind the pool is free all day Saturday.

85
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:27,038
Actually, I'd better not book it yet. My grandmother
sometimes goes to her bridge club on a Saturday, and I don't

86
00:06:27,062 --> 00:06:30,972
want to drive all that way if she isn't going to be
home. I'll ring her tonight and then book it in the app.

87
00:06:30,973 --> 00:06:34,960
No problem at all. I'll email you a
link to the app in the next few minutes.

88
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:36,960
Great. Thanks so much for your help, Craig.

89
00:06:37,210 --> 00:06:39,960
My pleasure, Joanna. Enjoy the drive.

90
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:42,776
That is the end of part one.

91
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:46,972
You now have one minute to
check your answers to part one.

92
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:10,959
Thank you.

93
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:10,960
Thank you.

94
